abstract: >
  The Interdependent Way is an indisciplinary ethical and psychological framework
  in active development. It integrates analytical psychology, empirical research
  on obedience and role adoption, and competence-based ethics to examine how
  interdependency, authority, and symbolic resonance shape human behavior.
